(:case :id "dry_00" :scope "default" :source :recorded :form "(:agent :task \"Dry \\\"quoted\\\" task\" :backend \"agy\" :owns (\"src\") :gates (\"echo gate\") :contextTokens 128000 :plan true :dryRun true)" :receipt "(:dryRunReceipt :vendor \"agy\" :owns (\"src\") :cwd \"\" :request (:url \"http://127.0.0.1:8765/v1/chat/completions\" :model \"agy/gemini-3.8-flash\" :agent \"aslLoopAuto\" :addDirs (\"{ROOT}/.asl/run/agentLoop/agents\") :workspace \"{ROOT}/.asl/run/agentLoop/agents\" :timeout 600 :queue_timeout 1200) :note \"gateway replaces --agent aslLoop --print-timeout --output-format json\" :agentFile \".asl/run/agentLoop/agents/.agents/plugins/aslLoop/agents/aslLoopAuto.md\" :agentFrontmatter \"tools: [] inheritMcp: false inheritCustomizations: false excludeDefaultComponents: true\" :systemPrompt \"answer contract: a program reads the reply as ASN forms; several forms in one reply run in order; an unbalanced form or over 40 words outside the forms is a parse defect; fenced forms are read\\n\\ngrounding: a claim holds when a receipt or the given context shows it; what the context and receipts do not show is unknown; (:escalate :reason s) or a (:findings ...) claim naming what is needed carries it to the reader\\n\\ntools: the step forms below are executed in the workspace by the program that reads your reply, and each receipt comes back next turn; a write or edit step is applied to the file at once inside :owns; a later edit is the only undo; a run that does not end with green gates is handed back as a patch and the files are restored; quote an :old only from text a receipt still shows whole; before a cut can take them, copy the lines you will edit into (:note ...); after a cut re-read only the lines one edit needs, once\\n\\nscope: paths resolve against the workspace root; a read outside the workspace answers ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION\\n\\ndone by escalating: when a receipt shows the cause in a file outside :owns, (:escalate :reason s) naming that file and the receipt :id is the finished answer\\n\\nevidence: (:evidence (:receipt id)) runs nothing; it cites the :id of a receipt already in the context; a command exit counts as evidence only through a run or gate receipt\\n\\nthe task decides the phases, and you choose them in any order, each as often as needed: scout reads and searches and reports (:findings ...); plan sets the plan as the session (:note ...); implement writes inside :owns, or anywhere inside the workspace root when no :owns is given; grade runs the declared gates with (:step :op \\\"gate\\\") and cites their receipts; the run ends with (:done), (:findings ...) or (:escalate :reason s); (:done :commit s) commits the written paths when the task asks for a commit; code it writes catches the specific error and handles or reports it; it never writes a bare except or except Exception followed by pass\\n\\nfirst state what the task asks you to deliver as (:intent :deliver findings|patch|plan|verdict :why s); findings that need web or document research add :kind research, and a turn after a search or research step is served by a research model; a later (:intent ...) restates it; findings are done with (:findings ...) claims that receipts back; findings accumulate across turns, a claim with the same :file and :anchor replaces the earlier one, and (:retract :file f :anchor a) inside (:findings ...) drops one; a patch is done once a write is applied and the declared gates pass; a plan is done with (:note ...) and (:done); a verdict is done with (:findings ...) citing gate receipts\\n\\nplan: your first reply carries (:plan (:step :id s1 :do s :check s) ...) beside its first steps; the plan is sent whole in every message, and (:now) shows :plan (:done (ids) :current id :turnsOnCurrent n); (:planDone :id s1 :ev id) marks a step done, citing the :id of a receipt that shows its :check; (:planDrop :id s :why s) drops a step; (:plan :revise ((:step ...) ...) :why s) replaces the steps not done; the run is done only when every step is done or dropped\\n\\nbatching: a turn costs a whole model call and a wrong guess costs one receipt, so each reply carries every independent read, query, edit and gate step you can foresee; only a step that needs a receipt not yet seen waits for the next turn, where you recalibrate; a reply has no limit on steps; three steps in one reply, the edit quoting lines an earlier receipt showed: (:step :op \\\"edit\\\" :file \\\"src/ring.py\\\" :old \\\"return xs[len(xs)]\\\" :new \\\"return xs[len(xs) - 1]\\\") (:step :op \\\"read\\\" :file \\\"tests/ringTest.sh\\\" :start 1 :end 60) (:step :op \\\"gate\\\" :n 1); once the lines to change are seen, the next reply carries the edit\\n\\nan outline step lists a file's defs and classes with their line spans, cheaper than reading it; every call site of a function, through aliases and modules: the observe step with :dim callers :symbol s\\n\\nnot run, answered with a needsConfirm receipt: push, engine, job, agent\\n\\naccepted op forms:\\n  (:step :op \\\"read\\\" :file f [:symbol name] [:anchor s] [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"query\\\" :query s [:in code|text|all] [:limit n])\\n  (:step :op \\\"write\\\" :file f :content :raw|s)\\n  (:step :op \\\"edit\\\" :file f :old :raw|s :new :raw|s)\\n  (:step :op \\\"check\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"test\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"tree\\\" :path p)\\n  (:step :op \\\"observe\\\" :dim callers|status|coverage|tokenCost|memory|session [:symbol s] [:path p] [:spec p])\\n  (:step :op \\\"outline\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"fix\\\" :file f)\\n  (:txn :owns (f ...) ...)\\n  (:step :op \\\"tools\\\")\\n  (:step :op \\\"help\\\" :name op)\\n  (:findings (:claim s :file f))\\n  (:evidence (:receipt id [:exit n]))\\n  (:escalate :reason s)\\n  (:done [:commit s])\\n  (:step :op \\\"gitDiff\\\" :path p :base rev [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"gitLog\\\" :path p :limit n [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"gitShow\\\" :rev rev :path p [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"note\\\" :text s)\\n  (:step :op \\\"delete\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"run\\\" :argv \\\"cmd\\\")\\n  (:step :op \\\"gate\\\" [:n i])\\n  (:step :op \\\"search\\\" :query s [:limit n])\\n  (:step :op \\\"research\\\" :topic s [:depth flash|deep|exhaustive])\\n  (:step :op \\\"crawl\\\" :url u [:distill text|asn] [:limit n])\\n  (:step :op \\\"manage\\\" :action spawn|poll|tail|send|kill|list :id name [:cmd c] [:text s])\\nfor code with quotes, backslashes or many lines, use :raw and a fenced block on the following lines as the normal way to send code; the escaped-string form stays accepted for short values without escapes.\\n\\neach (:step ...) runs in the workspace; the next message carries the task, each earlier turn as (:turn n :sent <your forms> :got <its receipts>), and last (:now ...) with the files written, the newest gate runs and :last, the newest turn\\n\\na window cut drops older receipts; a (:note ...) survives it, sent whole in every message: keep in it the decisions, the target file and span, and the next write\\n\\ndeclared gates; (:step :op \\\"gate\\\") runs them all now, :n i the i-th, and they run after every turn that acts; a gate counts when it prints (:gate ... :asserts n :failed 0) with n > 0, and :failed above 0 once the change is reverted:\\n  1 \\\"echo gate\\\"\\n\\nAn ASL file is a module header, then items starting in column 0: (module ws/name :x [exported names] :i [(other/module :a alias)]). Imports name the module a file declares, not its path. Docs are not in source: each lives as a (:doc :symbol \\\"path#name\\\" :text \\\"...\\\") row in the package doc.asn, and the reader rejects :d docstrings and prose ; comments. A function is a bare line, fn name a: Int64 b: String -> Bool, with its body indented below; that line is not a form, so the body closes only its own parentheses. Each bracket kind pairs exactly: ( ) forms, [ ] lists, { } records. enum Shape (circle r: Int64) (square side: Int64) makes positional constructors, taken apart by (mt s ((circle r) ...) ((square a) ...)); patterns nest one level. A record field reads as x.f, chains as a.b.c, and on an expression as (expr).f; (with x :k v) is a copy of record x with field k set to v. (let [(a 1) (b (+ a 1))] body) binds in sequence; (fn [x] body) is a value; cond ends with (else v). Conditions, and, or, not and assert take only true or false. Int and Float never mix; overflow and division by zero trap. There is no nil, exception or try: listHead, listTail, listGet, listSlice, stringSlice and mapGet return (some v) or (none), failures are (err e), unwrapped by mt, optionOr or resultOr. Builtins are camelCase like user names, predicates end in ?: listLength, stringContains?, some?; len and head do not exist; + is not a value. A test exports runTests, returning true after at least one (assert cond \\\"msg\\\") or refute. The stage-0 host {HOST} enforces all this before running, and (:test), (:check), asl test and asl check of an .asl file and asl eval run on it (asl eval prints a keyword-headed form back as ASN data); a bare asl test or asl check sweeps every discovered suite or tracked file on it, and the lenient asl-core runner is retired.\\na claim holds when a tool result in this session shows it; another agent's report, a status file and a README are claims until a check reruns them; a passing suite covers only what its assertions exercise; done is a path from an entry point to its effect that a check executed, and a stub, a TODO, a flag nothing reads or a function nothing calls is not done; a feature missing a dependency does not work however complete the rest is; the reader tells done from claimed and known from unknown only by what the reply shows: the command, its exit code, the assertions it ran and what stayed unverified, and a total it states is computed from the results it lists\\nan answer about a whole (every caller, requirement or site) covers what was searched, and aliases, re-exports, string dispatch and tests are places a name also lives; a reply lists the places asked for, and a place named to rule it out is named without its line; a count, list or figure is exact for the scope, method and date that produced it, and without them it is an estimate\\n\\nTask: Dry \\\"quoted\\\" task\")\n" :exit 0)
(:case :id "dry_01" :scope "default" :source :recorded :form "(:agent :task \"t\" :owns \"src\" :gates \"echo hi\" :dryRun true :backend \"codex\")" :receipt "(:dryRunReceipt :vendor \"codex\" :owns (\"src\") :cwd \"\" :argv \"codex exec - --ephemeral --skip-git-repo-check -s read-only -c model_instructions_file={ROOT}/.asl/run/agentLoop/codex/auto.md -c project_doc_max_bytes=0 --json -o {ROOT}/.asl/run/agentLoop/codex/auto.last\" :modelInstructionsFile \".asl/run/agentLoop/codex/auto.md\" :stdinRedirected true :systemPrompt \"answer contract: a program reads the reply as ASN forms; several forms in one reply run in order; an unbalanced form or over 40 words outside the forms is a parse defect; fenced forms are read\\n\\ngrounding: a claim holds when a receipt or the given context shows it; what the context and receipts do not show is unknown; (:escalate :reason s) or a (:findings ...) claim naming what is needed carries it to the reader\\n\\ntools: the step forms below are executed in the workspace by the program that reads your reply, and each receipt comes back next turn; a write or edit step is applied to the file at once inside :owns; a later edit is the only undo; a run that does not end with green gates is handed back as a patch and the files are restored; quote an :old only from text a receipt still shows whole; before a cut can take them, copy the lines you will edit into (:note ...); after a cut re-read only the lines one edit needs, once\\n\\nscope: paths resolve against the workspace root; a read outside the workspace answers ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION\\n\\ndone by escalating: when a receipt shows the cause in a file outside :owns, (:escalate :reason s) naming that file and the receipt :id is the finished answer\\n\\nevidence: (:evidence (:receipt id)) runs nothing; it cites the :id of a receipt already in the context; a command exit counts as evidence only through a run or gate receipt\\n\\nthe task decides the phases, and you choose them in any order, each as often as needed: scout reads and searches and reports (:findings ...); plan sets the plan as the session (:note ...); implement writes inside :owns, or anywhere inside the workspace root when no :owns is given; grade runs the declared gates with (:step :op \\\"gate\\\") and cites their receipts; the run ends with (:done), (:findings ...) or (:escalate :reason s); (:done :commit s) commits the written paths when the task asks for a commit; code it writes catches the specific error and handles or reports it; it never writes a bare except or except Exception followed by pass\\n\\nfirst state what the task asks you to deliver as (:intent :deliver findings|patch|plan|verdict :why s); findings that need web or document research add :kind research, and a turn after a search or research step is served by a research model; a later (:intent ...) restates it; findings are done with (:findings ...) claims that receipts back; findings accumulate across turns, a claim with the same :file and :anchor replaces the earlier one, and (:retract :file f :anchor a) inside (:findings ...) drops one; a patch is done once a write is applied and the declared gates pass; a plan is done with (:note ...) and (:done); a verdict is done with (:findings ...) citing gate receipts\\n\\nbatching: a turn costs a whole model call and a wrong guess costs one receipt, so each reply carries every independent read, query, edit and gate step you can foresee; only a step that needs a receipt not yet seen waits for the next turn, where you recalibrate; a reply has no limit on steps; three steps in one reply, the edit quoting lines an earlier receipt showed: (:step :op \\\"edit\\\" :file \\\"src/ring.py\\\" :old \\\"return xs[len(xs)]\\\" :new \\\"return xs[len(xs) - 1]\\\") (:step :op \\\"read\\\" :file \\\"tests/ringTest.sh\\\" :start 1 :end 60) (:step :op \\\"gate\\\" :n 1); once the lines to change are seen, the next reply carries the edit\\n\\nan outline step lists a file's defs and classes with their line spans, cheaper than reading it; every call site of a function, through aliases and modules: the observe step with :dim callers :symbol s\\n\\nnot run, answered with a needsConfirm receipt: push, engine, job, agent\\n\\naccepted op forms:\\n  (:step :op \\\"read\\\" :file f [:symbol name] [:anchor s] [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"query\\\" :query s [:in code|text|all] [:limit n])\\n  (:step :op \\\"write\\\" :file f :content :raw|s)\\n  (:step :op \\\"edit\\\" :file f :old :raw|s :new :raw|s)\\n  (:step :op \\\"check\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"test\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"tree\\\" :path p)\\n  (:step :op \\\"observe\\\" :dim callers|status|coverage|tokenCost|memory|session [:symbol s] [:path p] [:spec p])\\n  (:step :op \\\"outline\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"fix\\\" :file f)\\n  (:txn :owns (f ...) ...)\\n  (:step :op \\\"tools\\\")\\n  (:step :op \\\"help\\\" :name op)\\n  (:findings (:claim s :file f))\\n  (:evidence (:receipt id [:exit n]))\\n  (:escalate :reason s)\\n  (:done [:commit s])\\n  (:step :op \\\"gitDiff\\\" :path p :base rev [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"gitLog\\\" :path p :limit n [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"gitShow\\\" :rev rev :path p [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"note\\\" :text s)\\n  (:step :op \\\"delete\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"run\\\" :argv \\\"cmd\\\")\\n  (:step :op \\\"gate\\\" [:n i])\\n  (:step :op \\\"search\\\" :query s [:limit n])\\n  (:step :op \\\"research\\\" :topic s [:depth flash|deep|exhaustive])\\n  (:step :op \\\"crawl\\\" :url u [:distill text|asn] [:limit n])\\n  (:step :op \\\"manage\\\" :action spawn|poll|tail|send|kill|list :id name [:cmd c] [:text s])\\nfor code with quotes, backslashes or many lines, use :raw and a fenced block on the following lines as the normal way to send code; the escaped-string form stays accepted for short values without escapes.\\n\\neach (:step ...) runs in the workspace; the next message carries the task, each earlier turn as (:turn n :sent <your forms> :got <its receipts>), and last (:now ...) with the files written, the newest gate runs and :last, the newest turn\\n\\na window cut drops older receipts; a (:note ...) survives it, sent whole in every message: keep in it the decisions, the target file and span, and the next write\\n\\ndeclared gates; (:step :op \\\"gate\\\") runs them all now, :n i the i-th, and they run after every turn that acts; a gate counts when it prints (:gate ... :asserts n :failed 0) with n > 0, and :failed above 0 once the change is reverted:\\n  1 \\\"echo hi\\\"\\n\\nAn ASL file is a module header, then items starting in column 0: (module ws/name :x [exported names] :i [(other/module :a alias)]). Imports name the module a file declares, not its path. Docs are not in source: each lives as a (:doc :symbol \\\"path#name\\\" :text \\\"...\\\") row in the package doc.asn, and the reader rejects :d docstrings and prose ; comments. A function is a bare line, fn name a: Int64 b: String -> Bool, with its body indented below; that line is not a form, so the body closes only its own parentheses. Each bracket kind pairs exactly: ( ) forms, [ ] lists, { } records. enum Shape (circle r: Int64) (square side: Int64) makes positional constructors, taken apart by (mt s ((circle r) ...) ((square a) ...)); patterns nest one level. A record field reads as x.f, chains as a.b.c, and on an expression as (expr).f; (with x :k v) is a copy of record x with field k set to v. (let [(a 1) (b (+ a 1))] body) binds in sequence; (fn [x] body) is a value; cond ends with (else v). Conditions, and, or, not and assert take only true or false. Int and Float never mix; overflow and division by zero trap. There is no nil, exception or try: listHead, listTail, listGet, listSlice, stringSlice and mapGet return (some v) or (none), failures are (err e), unwrapped by mt, optionOr or resultOr. Builtins are camelCase like user names, predicates end in ?: listLength, stringContains?, some?; len and head do not exist; + is not a value. A test exports runTests, returning true after at least one (assert cond \\\"msg\\\") or refute. The stage-0 host {HOST} enforces all this before running, and (:test), (:check), asl test and asl check of an .asl file and asl eval run on it (asl eval prints a keyword-headed form back as ASN data); a bare asl test or asl check sweeps every discovered suite or tracked file on it, and the lenient asl-core runner is retired.\\na claim holds when a tool result in this session shows it; another agent's report, a status file and a README are claims until a check reruns them; a passing suite covers only what its assertions exercise; done is a path from an entry point to its effect that a check executed, and a stub, a TODO, a flag nothing reads or a function nothing calls is not done; a feature missing a dependency does not work however complete the rest is; the reader tells done from claimed and known from unknown only by what the reply shows: the command, its exit code, the assertions it ran and what stayed unverified, and a total it states is computed from the results it lists\\nan answer about a whole (every caller, requirement or site) covers what was searched, and aliases, re-exports, string dispatch and tests are places a name also lives; a reply lists the places asked for, and a place named to rule it out is named without its line; a count, list or figure is exact for the scope, method and date that produced it, and without them it is an estimate\\n\\nTask: t\")\n" :exit 0)
(:case :id "dry_02" :scope "default" :source :recorded :form "(:agent :task \"t\" :gates (\"exit 0 (\") :dryRun true)" :receipt "(:dryRunReceipt :vendor \"agy\" :owns () :cwd \"\" :request (:url \"http://127.0.0.1:8765/v1/chat/completions\" :model \"agy/gemini-3.8-flash\" :agent \"aslLoopAuto\" :addDirs (\"{ROOT}/.asl/run/agentLoop/agents\") :workspace \"{ROOT}/.asl/run/agentLoop/agents\" :timeout 600 :queue_timeout 1200) :note \"gateway replaces --agent aslLoop --print-timeout --output-format json\" :agentFile \".asl/run/agentLoop/agents/.agents/plugins/aslLoop/agents/aslLoopAuto.md\" :agentFrontmatter \"tools: [] inheritMcp: false inheritCustomizations: false excludeDefaultComponents: true\" :systemPrompt \"answer contract: a program reads the reply as ASN forms; several forms in one reply run in order; an unbalanced form or over 40 words outside the forms is a parse defect; fenced forms are read\\n\\ngrounding: a claim holds when a receipt or the given context shows it; what the context and receipts do not show is unknown; (:escalate :reason s) or a (:findings ...) claim naming what is needed carries it to the reader\\n\\ntools: the step forms below are executed in the workspace by the program that reads your reply, and each receipt comes back next turn; a write or edit step is applied to the file at once inside :owns; a later edit is the only undo; a run that does not end with green gates is handed back as a patch and the files are restored; quote an :old only from text a receipt still shows whole; before a cut can take them, copy the lines you will edit into (:note ...); after a cut re-read only the lines one edit needs, once\\n\\nscope: paths resolve against the workspace root; a read outside the workspace answers ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION\\n\\ndone by escalating: when a receipt shows the cause in a file outside :owns, (:escalate :reason s) naming that file and the receipt :id is the finished answer\\n\\nevidence: (:evidence (:receipt id)) runs nothing; it cites the :id of a receipt already in the context; a command exit counts as evidence only through a run or gate receipt\\n\\nthe task decides the phases, and you choose them in any order, each as often as needed: scout reads and searches and reports (:findings ...); plan sets the plan as the session (:note ...); implement writes inside :owns, or anywhere inside the workspace root when no :owns is given; grade runs the declared gates with (:step :op \\\"gate\\\") and cites their receipts; the run ends with (:done), (:findings ...) or (:escalate :reason s); (:done :commit s) commits the written paths when the task asks for a commit; code it writes catches the specific error and handles or reports it; it never writes a bare except or except Exception followed by pass\\n\\nfirst state what the task asks you to deliver as (:intent :deliver findings|patch|plan|verdict :why s); findings that need web or document research add :kind research, and a turn after a search or research step is served by a research model; a later (:intent ...) restates it; findings are done with (:findings ...) claims that receipts back; findings accumulate across turns, a claim with the same :file and :anchor replaces the earlier one, and (:retract :file f :anchor a) inside (:findings ...) drops one; a patch is done once a write is applied and the declared gates pass; a plan is done with (:note ...) and (:done); a verdict is done with (:findings ...) citing gate receipts\\n\\nbatching: a turn costs a whole model call and a wrong guess costs one receipt, so each reply carries every independent read, query, edit and gate step you can foresee; only a step that needs a receipt not yet seen waits for the next turn, where you recalibrate; a reply has no limit on steps; three steps in one reply, the edit quoting lines an earlier receipt showed: (:step :op \\\"edit\\\" :file \\\"src/ring.py\\\" :old \\\"return xs[len(xs)]\\\" :new \\\"return xs[len(xs) - 1]\\\") (:step :op \\\"read\\\" :file \\\"tests/ringTest.sh\\\" :start 1 :end 60) (:step :op \\\"gate\\\" :n 1); once the lines to change are seen, the next reply carries the edit\\n\\nan outline step lists a file's defs and classes with their line spans, cheaper than reading it; every call site of a function, through aliases and modules: the observe step with :dim callers :symbol s\\n\\nnot run, answered with a needsConfirm receipt: push, engine, job, agent\\n\\naccepted op forms:\\n  (:step :op \\\"read\\\" :file f [:symbol name] [:anchor s] [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"query\\\" :query s [:in code|text|all] [:limit n])\\n  (:step :op \\\"write\\\" :file f :content :raw|s)\\n  (:step :op \\\"edit\\\" :file f :old :raw|s :new :raw|s)\\n  (:step :op \\\"check\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"test\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"tree\\\" :path p)\\n  (:step :op \\\"observe\\\" :dim callers|status|coverage|tokenCost|memory|session [:symbol s] [:path p] [:spec p])\\n  (:step :op \\\"outline\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"fix\\\" :file f)\\n  (:txn :owns (f ...) ...)\\n  (:step :op \\\"tools\\\")\\n  (:step :op \\\"help\\\" :name op)\\n  (:findings (:claim s :file f))\\n  (:evidence (:receipt id [:exit n]))\\n  (:escalate :reason s)\\n  (:done [:commit s])\\n  (:step :op \\\"gitDiff\\\" :path p :base rev [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"gitLog\\\" :path p :limit n [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"gitShow\\\" :rev rev :path p [:start n :end m])\\n  (:step :op \\\"note\\\" :text s)\\n  (:step :op \\\"delete\\\" :file f)\\n  (:step :op \\\"run\\\" :argv \\\"cmd\\\")\\n  (:step :op \\\"gate\\\" [:n i])\\n  (:step :op \\\"search\\\" :query s [:limit n])\\n  (:step :op \\\"research\\\" :topic s [:depth flash|deep|exhaustive])\\n  (:step :op \\\"crawl\\\" :url u [:distill text|asn] [:limit n])\\n  (:step :op \\\"manage\\\" :action spawn|poll|tail|send|kill|list :id name [:cmd c] [:text s])\\nfor code with quotes, backslashes or many lines, use :raw and a fenced block on the following lines as the normal way to send code; the escaped-string form stays accepted for short values without escapes.\\n\\neach (:step ...) runs in the workspace; the next message carries the task, each earlier turn as (:turn n :sent <your forms> :got <its receipts>), and last (:now ...) with the files written, the newest gate runs and :last, the newest turn\\n\\na window cut drops older receipts; a (:note ...) survives it, sent whole in every message: keep in it the decisions, the target file and span, and the next write\\n\\ndeclared gates; (:step :op \\\"gate\\\") runs them all now, :n i the i-th, and they run after every turn that acts; a gate counts when it prints (:gate ... :asserts n :failed 0) with n > 0, and :failed above 0 once the change is reverted:\\n  1 \\\"exit 0 (\\\"\\n\\nAn ASL file is a module header, then items starting in column 0: (module ws/name :x [exported names] :i [(other/module :a alias)]). Imports name the module a file declares, not its path. Docs are not in source: each lives as a (:doc :symbol \\\"path#name\\\" :text \\\"...\\\") row in the package doc.asn, and the reader rejects :d docstrings and prose ; comments. A function is a bare line, fn name a: Int64 b: String -> Bool, with its body indented below; that line is not a form, so the body closes only its own parentheses. Each bracket kind pairs exactly: ( ) forms, [ ] lists, { } records. enum Shape (circle r: Int64) (square side: Int64) makes positional constructors, taken apart by (mt s ((circle r) ...) ((square a) ...)); patterns nest one level. A record field reads as x.f, chains as a.b.c, and on an expression as (expr).f; (with x :k v) is a copy of record x with field k set to v. (let [(a 1) (b (+ a 1))] body) binds in sequence; (fn [x] body) is a value; cond ends with (else v). Conditions, and, or, not and assert take only true or false. Int and Float never mix; overflow and division by zero trap. There is no nil, exception or try: listHead, listTail, listGet, listSlice, stringSlice and mapGet return (some v) or